.git* export-ignore
cmake/Version.cmake export-subst
# One line ending in the tree: LF. A file a Windows editor saved with
# CRLF is normalised on commit, and a checkout on Windows gets LF, so a
# fixture `include_str!`-ed or compared byte-for-byte reads the same on
# every platform (DAEMON_CONFIG_CUTOVER.md DC-F40, DC-F42). The product
# does not depend on it: `shekyld` reads a CRLF `shekyld.toml` as it
# reads an LF one (`a_crlf_file_builds_what_its_lf_twin_builds`). The
# `-text` entries below are exempt, each for its own reason.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Captured as CRLF or mixed before this rule and kept as captured: a
# benchmark record, a quoted upstream issue. Not renormalised.
docs/benchmarks/rt_p4_mlkem_decaps_timing_20261011_captures/laptop_samples.tsv -text
docs/benchmarks/rt_p4_mlkem_decaps_timing_20261023_captures/example_rustc_line.txt -text
docs/benchmarks/rt_p4_mlkem_decaps_timing_20261023_captures/laptop_x86_disasm_excerpts_crt_static.txt -text
docs/design/refs/zawy12_issue_24_history.md -text
docs/design/refs/zawy12_issue_3_lwma1.md -text
docs/design/refs/zawy12_issue_3_lwma3.md -text
# KAT corpora are byte-load-bearing fixtures (ADDRESS_DERIVATION_V1 is
# hash-pinned via include_str! in address_derivation_freeze.rs). Never
# apply EOL conversion: working-tree bytes must equal committed bytes.
docs/test_vectors/** -text
# RPC oracle vectors (docs/completed/DAEMON_RPC_KV_CUTOVER.md §3.5): epee's exact
# bytes, CRLF included. Never apply EOL conversion.
rust/shekyl-rpc-types/tests/vectors/rpc/** -text
# The `.bin` vectors are portable_storage, not text: keep them out of
# textual diffs too, so a reviewer sees "binary files differ" rather than a
# mangled rendering that invites an edit. `-text` is already applied above.
rust/shekyl-rpc-types/tests/vectors/rpc/*.bin -diff
# Frozen numeric oracle (`the_long_term_weight_follows_the_generators_trajectory`).
# A trailing CR fails the last field's parse, and that panic is the failure.
# Checkout must not rewrite the line endings.
rust/shekyl-chain-rules/tests/vectors/block_weight_trajectory/trajectory.txt -text
